cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to twinflow in academic or professional work, please cite it using this metadata."
title: twinflow
abstract: >-
  twinflow is a digital twin of a warehouse receiving-and-putaway operation
  that stays synchronized with a simulated IoT device fleet over MQTT. Devices
  publish Sparkplug B payloads into an ISA-95 Unified Namespace, a historian
  records the stream, machine learning detects anomalies and locates throughput
  constraints, and a Lean Six Sigma statistical engine judges both the telemetry
  and the twin continuously using SPC, process capability, measurement system
  analysis, hypothesis testing, and process mining. An AI agent answers
  operational questions and runs what-if experiments against the twin, grounding
  every number in an executed query rather than generating it. All data is
  synthetic and generated by the repository itself, the system runs locally with
  no cloud account, and every run is reproducible from a single seed.
type: software
